    {
      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "10cm — My Eyes",
      "content": "Things that happen gradually or beyond your control. \"I ended up loving you.\"\n\nMy Eyes is a 10cm song about the exact moment someone realizes they've fallen for a person — not gradually, but suddenly, with almost alarming intensity. The narrator can't hear anything except this person's voice, can't see anything except their eyes, and genuinely wonders out loud whether he's lost his mind.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-게 되다**, which means \"to end up ~ing.\" We'll see how 10cm uses it in \"My Eyes.\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **목소리** — voice\n- **보이다** — to be seen\n- **목소리가 들리다** — a voice can be heard\n- **좋아하게 되다** — to end up liking\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
